  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet",
      "indent": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The exposé should focus on specific, well-defined research questions, and describe experiments that tackle these questions in great detail. The research question and subquestions are stated but formulated as broad and general questions. Subsequently, the approach chapter does not contain a clear description of the experimental setup, but only contains general directions, like „do an interview with students“, or „use software like Python“. The exposé would improve a lot by narrowing the scope and covering fewer research questions in more detail."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "indent": 2,
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "Limited Bibliography:",
    "attributes": {
      "bold": true
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet",
      "indent": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The exposé should contain an appropriate amount of citations, covering foundational work and recent approaches that the exposé can compare with. While the bibliography contains foundational and relevant references, it could be expanded to include more recent and diverse studies on LLMs in education, personalized learning, and related fields. Overall, one reference is wrong, two references are general and not very recent (2016 and 2007), and the last reference is a website. More references would provide a stronger grounding for the proposed research."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "indent": 2,
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "Underdeveloped Metrics Definition:",
    "attributes": {
      "bold": true
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet",
      "indent": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The concept of metrics is central to the research, yet the exposé could provide a more detailed discussion of potential metrics (e.g., specific engagement indicators or learning outcome measures). This would strengthen the methodological foundation."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
